  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Regional Migration Response Plan for the Horn of Africa and Yemen</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Horn of Africa and Yemen is a region of origin, transit, and destination for hundreds of thousands of migrants, the majority of whom travel in an irregular manner, often relying on smugglers to facilitate movement along the Eastern Route (originating from Ethiopia and Somalia and transiting through Somalia, Djibouti, and Yemen) with the intention of crossing the Gulf of Aden towards the Gulf States to seek better livelihood opportunities. The vulnerabilities of the migrants are one of the specific drivers to migration and determinants of IOM&apos;s response through the Regional Migrants Response Plan. Through this project, IOM is providing life-saving assistance to vulnerable migrants and host communities including protection assistance and services.</narrative>
  </description>
